<title>JAPAN: Toho Zinc plans higher lead, zinc output.</title>
<headline>Toho Zinc plans higher lead, zinc output.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-10-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>Toho Zinc Co said on Tuesday it planned to produce slightly more refined lead and zinc in the half-year to March 1997 than in the same period a year ago.</p>
<p>Zinc output was planned at 67,565 tonnes, up from 64,315 tonnes during the same period the year before and an estimated 64,164 tonnes in the first half of this year.</p>
<p>Projected lead output was 48,000 tonnes, up from 46,884 tonnes during the same period last year and an estimated 42,100 tonnes in the first half of this year.</p>
<p>The forecasts include Toho's share of output from jointly owned zinc refineries and metal refined for other companies on a tolling basis.</p>
<p>-- Tokyo Commodities Desk (81-3 3432 6179)</p>
</text>
